  "term": "parole",
  "definition": "In this historical psychology source, parole refers to internal speech: the mental revival of speech, with or without actual speaking. It covers experiences like silently having words in mind, musing, or mentally hearing tunes, and includes the role these inner revivals play in speaking or singing.",
